---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy | Chip & Cell"
  description="What Chip & Cell collects, what it does not, and how advertising and analytics cookies are used on this site."
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: September 21, 2026</p>

  <p>
    Chip &amp; Cell does not have user accounts, newsletters or comment forms. We do not ask
    you for your name, email address or any other personal detail in order to read the site,
    and we do not sell or rent visitor data to anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>What is collected automatically</h2>
  <p>
    Like any website, our host records standard server request data — IP address, browser
    and device type, referring page and the URL requested. This is used to keep the site
    running and to measure aggregate traffic. We do not use it to build a profile of you.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    This site is supported by advertising. We use Google AdSense. Google and its partners
    are third-party vendors that may use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to
    this or other websites, and may collect data such as your IP address, browser type and
    the pages you view here in order to select and measure those ads.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can turn off personalised advertising in
    <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>.
    You can opt out of third-party vendor cookies at
    <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>, or, in the
    EU and UK, at <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="noopener">Your Online Choices</a>.
    See also
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener">how Google uses cookies in advertising</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use aggregate traffic analytics to see which pages are read. We do not store
    information that identifies you personally.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings at any time; the site remains
    fully readable without them. If you are in the EEA, UK or California and want to know
    what data our advertising partner holds, follow the Google links above — that data sits
    with Google, not with us.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the date at the top of this page changes with it.
    Questions: see our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .muted { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
</style>
